solution:
The denominator \(3\) in the exponent tells us to use the real cube root. Since \((-1/5)^3=-1/125\), and a negative exponent means taking a reciprocal,
\[
\left(-\frac1{125}\right)^{-2/3}
=\left(-\frac15\right)^{-2}
=\frac{1}{(-1/5)^2}
=\boxed{25}.
\]
The base is nonzero, so the reciprocal is defined. The answer is \(25\), choice \(\boxed{\text{C}}\).

